A||||3||zeusrekning||a lot of 2.8/3.4 questions.||||5||
Z||000000||zeusrekning||11-07-2000||06:46 PM||||I was wondering a few things. <BR>Car: 87 coupe 5 speed. engine hopefully 3.4<BR>1. My isuzu 5 speed will fit on the 3.4<BR>2. I'll need the engine and wireing harness out of the 2.8 donor right?<BR>3. What are the most high performance heads.<BR> 3.1 does the 3.1 have alum heads? My     neighbor has a lumina z34 with 3.1<BR>4.coolant hose same on the 87. I heard for an 88 you have to do some cutting.<BR>5.It really doen't seem that hard. guess sense i have not done it but what is the hardest thing for a 2.5 TO 3.5 swap.<P>^ not trying to start anything on this question but can you run a turbo and nitrous. I have a dream to go to comerce ga <BR>and kick some ricer @$$. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||11-07-2000||08:21 PM||||1, Y<BR>2, Y<BR>3, Your fiero 2.8 or Camaro 3.4 heads. The 3.1-liter engines had both cast iron heads and aluminum heads. The aluminum heads won't work with the fiero intake manifolds.<BR>4, I don't know but I have an 88 formula, which is getting a 3.4 transplant and there is no cutting of the coolant hoses involved.<BR>5, drilling the starter holes are the biggest hurdle. You can talk to fieroshop about doing it yourself. The rest is easy.<BR>Yes you can run both a turbo and nitrous. You can use the nitrous to give you the initial kick until the turbo builds its boost. <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/freddysplace/Page1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/freddysplace/Page1.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.paceparts.com/ht43.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.paceparts.com/ht43.htm</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.norrisracingtech.com/home.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.norrisracingtech.com/home.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.s-series.org/htm/windstorm/project-windstorm-stage3.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.s-series.org/htm/windstorm/project-windstorm-stage3.htm</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://members.home.net/sprigint/x11p/x11p.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.net/sprigint/x11p/x11p.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/3400engine.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/3400engine.htm</A> <P>Read on!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||11-08-2000||12:57 AM||||yes your 5-speed will bolt up to the 3.4. What you need from the 2.8 donor engine is basically everything from the heads up -- this will all bolt on to the 3.4. No cutting of the coolant lines is necessary but yes, you will have to move the starter to the other side of the 3.4 block from where it originally was mounted. We have a jig here for drilling the mounting holes. We just finished another 3.4 swap tonight and let me tell you it sounds GOOD!! and........lots and lots of torque!!<P>You didn't say whether you have the 2.5 or the 2.8 now but changing from a 2.5 to a 3.4 is slightly more involved but - make sure you get the wiring harness from the 2.8 as well as the computer!!<P>------------------<BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                            <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT<BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group<BR><A HREF="http://www.http://www.fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>www.http://www.fieroshop.net/</A> - Fiero Shop - Richmond, CA - 1-510-23-FIERO||||reg||1
Z||000003||zeusrekning||11-08-2000||05:44 AM||||ihave the 2.5 right now.||||reg||1
